<DocLayout
  title="Missing signals"
  description="Why Image Identifier often finds no credentials or empty file details — and why that is not proof of authenticity."
  updated="2026-10-14"
>
  <p>
    Many everyday photos have no recorded credentials and little or no useful file detail. Platforms
    strip fields; cameras differ; edits rewrite headers. Empty results are normal.
  </p>

  <h2>What missing evidence is not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Not proof the image is authentic.</li>
    <li>Not proof the image is AI-generated.</li>
    <li>Not proof nobody edited the file.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What to do next</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Check whether any module failed versus simply found nothing.</li>
    <li>Look for conflicting clues if some signals exist and others do not.</li>
    <li>Use other context outside this tool when stakes are high.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Related: <a href="/limits/">Provenance limits</a> and
    <a href="/guides/credentials/">Content credentials</a>.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
